a  administration did implement reforms  including banning the sale of some  military equipment to police and opening  over two dozen federal investigations  into law enforcement offices across the  country the  administration rolled much of that back  at a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing  Democrats blasted the order there is  nothing about what the president  announced today that would hold police  officers who break the rules and break  the law accountable the president  signaled he would be willing to work  with Congress on more significant  reforms and later today Senate Majority  Leader Mitch McConnell and Senator Tim  Scott will hold a press conference to  discuss their own police reform  proposals  Anthony Paula thank you
 

